WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:07.600
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain the American comedy-drama film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:15.920
called “The Truman Show.” Spoilers&nbsp;
ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:23.760
Truman Burbank leads a quiet and peaceful life&nbsp;
in Seahaven island, his birthplace. He is married&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:30.480
to a nurse named Meryl and works as an insurance&nbsp;
salesman. One day, as he is heading to work after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.480
greeting his neighbors across the street with his&nbsp;
traditional greeting, "Good morning! And in case I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:40.880
don't see you, good afternoon, good evening, and&nbsp;
good night", a strange object falls from the sky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:46.480
and lands near his car. He tries to ascertain&nbsp;
where it came from but doesn’t find any answers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:52.720
as the sky is clear and the object seems like&nbsp;
a studio light. He brushes it aside and drives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:58.480
to work. On his way to work, the radio reports&nbsp;
that an aircraft flying over the Seahaven island&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.560
shed its parts, which makes him believe&nbsp;
it was the source of the object. 
 
&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:08.240
At work, he makes a secret call to Fiji and asks&nbsp;
for information about a woman named Lauren/Silvia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:15.120
Garland. When he fails to find any information,&nbsp;
he leaves to close a deal on Harbor Island for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:20.560
his boss Lawrence. However, his fear of open&nbsp;
water gets to him, and he returns home.
 
&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.800
Later, he meets his childhood best friend Marlon&nbsp;
and confides in him his wish to leave everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:32.560
behind and move to Fiji. Ever since Truman&nbsp;
was a child, he wished to explore the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.800
but due to one thing or another, he never&nbsp;
got to go beyond Seahaven island.
 
&nbsp;

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:42.080
After Marlon leaves, Truman sits by the beach&nbsp;
alone and remembers a boating accident because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:48.240
of which he lost his father, Kirk Burbank. On that&nbsp;
fateful day, Truman’s father wanted to return from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:54.160
home early due to the bad weather, but Truman&nbsp;
insisted on staying out at sea for a bit longer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.160 --> 00:02:00.160
Lo and behold, a strong storm hit their boat,&nbsp;
and Mr. Burbank got swept overboard and drowned.
&nbsp;

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:06.880
As Truman snaps out of his memory, a strange&nbsp;
thing happens. It begins to rain but only on him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.680
He stands up in astonishment, and it begins&nbsp;
to rain everywhere. He rushes home and shares&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:17.120
his plans about moving to Fiji with Meryl, but&nbsp;
she dismisses the idea, citing their financial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:22.160
obligations and plans to have a baby. 
 
The next day, Truman runs into a homeless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:26.960
man on the street who looks just like his&nbsp;
father. But before he could talk to the man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:33.120
a number of people and obstacles show up, and the&nbsp;
man is dragged into a bus and taken away. Truman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.160
shares the incident with his mother, but Mrs.&nbsp;
Burbank dismisses it as Truman’s imagination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.520
She tells him that she too sees Mr. Burnbank&nbsp;
in strangers sometimes, and it is normal.
&nbsp;

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:49.120
That night, Truman goes into his basement and&nbsp;
looks through his old personal belongings hidden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.800
away in an old trunk. The trunk contains pictures&nbsp;
of his childhood and a red ladies’ sweater with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:00.080
pin that says, “How will it end?”. The sweater&nbsp;
takes him back to his college days when he saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:05.600
a beautiful young woman named Lauren Garland while&nbsp;
playing in the homecoming band with Marlon. Before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:11.120
he could court her, Lauren disappeared, and over&nbsp;
time, Truman got romantically close to Meryl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:16.400
However, one evening, Truman again runs into&nbsp;
Lauren in the library. He approaches her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:22.160
but she tells him that she’s not allowed to speak&nbsp;
with him. Despite this, Truman, smitten by her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:27.200
asks her if she’d go out with him on the weekends.&nbsp;
However, she tells him that she can only go out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:32.240
now, and the two try to head out of the library&nbsp;
secretly. The cameras in the library lose them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:37.120
for a second but eventually capture them running&nbsp;
out together through an alternative exit. 
&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:42.800
The pair make out on the beach, but suddenly a&nbsp;
vehicle approaches them, causing Lauren to panic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:47.440
She tells Truman that her real name is actually&nbsp;
Sylvia and tries to tell him the truth about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:52.400
“The Truman Show.” As the man, claiming&nbsp;
to be Mr. Garland tries to drag her away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:59.200
Lauren tells Truman that everything and everyone&nbsp;
around him is fake and part of a reality TV show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.440
The man calls Lauren “schizophrenic” and&nbsp;
takes her away, announcing that they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:09.120
moving to Fiji. Truman watches in confusion&nbsp;
with the red sweater that Lauren left behind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:14.320
After he returns back to reality, Truman pieces&nbsp;
together scraps of magazine pages to create a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:19.760
collage of Sylvia’s face as he remembers it.
 
The next day, on his way to work, the radio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:26.160
malfunctions and oddly reports every movement he&nbsp;
makes as if he is being watched. Soon, the radio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:31.280
again starts playing music after apologizing&nbsp;
for picking up the police’s frequency. 
&nbsp;

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:37.120
Paranoid, Truman rushes into a random building to&nbsp;
catch the people conspiring against him slipping.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.080
As he heads towards an elevator, he is&nbsp;
surprised to see what seems to be a TV studio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.120
filled with people wearing&nbsp;
headphones and eating lunch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.200
instead of an elevator car. Before he could&nbsp;
wrap his head around what he is seeing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:54.240
the security arrives and kicks him out&nbsp;
for trespassing. Confused, he meets Marlon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:59.360
and tells him about the strange occurrences.&nbsp;
However, Marlon dismisses it as his imagination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:04.400
Nevertheless, Truman confides in Marlon that&nbsp;
he is going to go away for a while. 
 
&nbsp;

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:11.200
When Truman returns home, he finds his mother and&nbsp;
Meryl watching old photos of them while on the TV,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:16.640
a show called ‘Show Me the Way to Go Home’ is&nbsp;
playing. It seems everyone is indirectly trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:21.360
to dissuade him from going on an exploration.&nbsp;
Truman suddenly notices his wedding picture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:26.320
where Meryl has her fingers crossed, implying&nbsp;
that Meryl didn’t marry him truthfully. 
 
&nbsp;

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:31.360
The next day, Truman proceeds to travel to Fiji&nbsp;
but learns that there are no available flights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:36.400
for at least a month. He then catches a bus to&nbsp;
Chicago, but the bus breaks down before it even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:41.600
gets to leave the station. Meryl returns home&nbsp;
from work and finds Truman sitting in his car.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:45.920
He invites her to sit next to him and&nbsp;
correctly predicts a chain of events-&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:51.760
a lady on a red bike, a man with flowers,&nbsp;
and a Volkswagen beetle with a dented fender.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.840
He claims that everything around him&nbsp;
is scripted, but she dismisses him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:01.040
As she proceeds to leave, Truman locks the car&nbsp;
door and starts driving around spontaneously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:06.080
to prove his theory. He proceeds to drive out of&nbsp;
the island, but the fear of open water takes over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:10.560
him, and he stops on the bridge which connects&nbsp;
Seahaven island to the rest of the country. 
&nbsp;

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:15.520
Determined to leave, he shuts his eyes&nbsp;
and slams his foot on the accelerator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:20.240
forcing Meryl to drive. They successfully&nbsp;
cross the bridge and continue on their journey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.360
but they are soon forced to stop by police just&nbsp;
before a nuclear power plant that seems to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:31.440
had a meltdown. A police officer orders him to&nbsp;
retreat but accidentally calls Truman by his first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:36.480
name despite having never met him before.
Convinced of foul play, Truman attempts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:40.720
to run out of the island, but the men&nbsp;
capture him and send him back home. 
 
&nbsp;

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:44.480
Back at home, Meryl tries to convince him&nbsp;
that everything is fine, but Truman gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:49.760
even more paranoid. Suddenly, Marlon appears&nbsp;
at the door and takes Truman out for a beer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:55.680
Marlon assures him that everyone is not conspiring&nbsp;
against him. Marons further adds, if everyone did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:00.720
he would have to be a co-conspirator, too, but&nbsp;
he can never lie to his best friend. It is then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:06.080
revealed that a man named Christof is feeding&nbsp;
these lines to Marlon through an earpiece. 
 
&nbsp;

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:10.880
Marlon then reveals the real reason he brought&nbsp;
him over for beer, and a man then appears from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:15.600
the mist. It is revealed to be the homeless&nbsp;
man that Truman was convinced is his father.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:20.480
It turns out he was right. It is Mr.&nbsp;
Burbank who Marlon found on the island.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:26.160
The father and son embrace as Christof instructs&nbsp;
his camera crew to beautifully capture the moment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:30.880
Mr. Burbank tearfully promises his son&nbsp;
to make up for the time they lost.
 
&nbsp;

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:37.280
It is finally confirmed that Truman is the star&nbsp;
of the most popular live show in TV history called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:44.000
“The Truman Show.” Unbeknownst to him, Truman’s&nbsp;
hometown, the Seahaven island, is a massive TV set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:49.440
surrounded by a dome that produces sophisticated&nbsp;
effects and imagery to mimic the sky, weather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:54.000
and temperature of the real world. The&nbsp;
dome is run by a huge staff under the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:59.920
command of the eccentric Director Christof. 
 
In an interview, Christof reveals Kirk Burbank is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:04.640
not the first one to enter the show without being&nbsp;
a part of the script, and there have been several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:09.840
attempts by fans to meet Truman. It is also&nbsp;
revealed that Christof previously killed Kirk’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:16.000
character to implant fear of water in Truman so&nbsp;
he wouldn’t think of leaving the island. Truman's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:21.840
birth was a case of unwanted pregnancy, and he&nbsp;
was the first child to be adopted by a corporation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:28.400
for a TV show. The show runs 24\7 and generates&nbsp;
revenues by product placements. While taking fan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:33.440
questions, Christof gets an angry call from Sylvia&nbsp;
Garland, who berates him for imprisoning Truman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:38.320
without his consent. Christof retorts by saying&nbsp;
that the real world is the actual prison while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:43.840
the “cell” Truman lives in gives him the chance&nbsp;
to lead a completely normal life, free of violence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:48.720
or pain. He finishes by adding that Truman is&nbsp;
free to leave should he discover the truth.
 
&nbsp;

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:51.680
The next day, Truman seems to&nbsp;
have gone back to his normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.840
self. However, Meryl leaves him because of his&nbsp;
paranoid behavior. At work, he is introduced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:59.520
to a new coworker named Vivien, appointed by&nbsp;
Christof as Truman’s prospective female partner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:04.480
Later that evening, Truman falls asleep in a&nbsp;
makeshift bed in his basement while organizing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:09.920
things. After several hours of inactivity,&nbsp;
Christof grows worried and orders the crew to ring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:16.000
Truman’s phone. However, Truman doesn’t answer,&nbsp;
much less move. Christof then sends Marlon over to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:20.880
his home with a pack of beer. Christof guides him&nbsp;
to the basement, and to everyone’s astonishment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:26.480
it is revealed that Truman is absent from his bed.&nbsp;
Marlon then discovers a large hole in the basement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:31.520
leading to the lawn. Truman has managed to&nbsp;
escape. With nothing to show to the audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:36.880
Christof cuts the live transmission for the&nbsp;
first time ever in the history of the show. 
 
&nbsp;

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:42.400
The cease in the transmission of the iconic show&nbsp;
sends shockwaves around the world. Pressure from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:49.040
fans, media, investors, and sponsors is kicking&nbsp;
Christof’s ass. He orders the entire staff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:54.480
including the extra actors, to go on a manhunt.&nbsp;
However, the actors find it hard to find a man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:59.840
in the dark. So, Christof orders the sun to&nbsp;
rise well before the actual time of sunrise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:05.440
to aid in Truman’s search. After searching every&nbsp;
inch of the land, Christof’s intuition tells him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:11.280
to check the sea surrounding the island. It works,&nbsp;
and the cameras spot Truman on a sailboat with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:17.280
a picture of Sylvia. The live transmission&nbsp;
is again resumed. At home, Sylva is elated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:21.840
to see Truman trying to find the truth.
 
Christof orders the ferry captain to fetch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:27.040
Truman but being just an actor; he doesn’t know&nbsp;
how to man a boat. Left with no other choice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:33.120
Christof simulates a storm to force Truman to go&nbsp;
back to port. Christof leaves no stone unturned to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:38.800
scare Truman, but he puts up a fight and defiantly&nbsp;
yells at the sky, “Is that the best you can do?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:43.680
You are gonna have to kill me.”
 
Enraged, Christoff sends sea wave after sea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:49.280
wave to break Truman, almost capsizing the boat&nbsp;
and nearly drowning Truman. Christof realizes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:56.320
Truman would rather die than concede and allows&nbsp;
the sky to clear. Truman continues to sail away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.320 --> 00:11:01.760
Soon, his boat is rocked by a strong impact.&nbsp;
Truman learns that his boat has collided with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:07.680
sky wall. He has reached the end of the dome. He&nbsp;
breaks into tears of joy. Walking on the edge of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:13.760
the sky, he reaches a staircase leading to an exit&nbsp;
door. As he proceeds to exit, Christof finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:19.360
speaks to Truman through the intercom and informs&nbsp;
him that he is the star of a reality TV show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:24.480
called “The Truman Show.” He tries to convince&nbsp;
Truman to continue to live on his fantasy island&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:30.240
as Sylvia and the entire world watch&nbsp;
intently on their TV set. Christof tells him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:36.080
“There's no more truth out there in the world than&nbsp;
I created for you. The same lies. The same deceit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:40.960
But in my world you have nothing to fear. ”
 
After some deliberation, Truman looks up at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:47.120
sky and says, “In case I don't see you, good&nbsp;
afternoon, good evening, and good night.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:52.480
before bowing and leaving. An elated Sylvia&nbsp;
rushes out of her apartment in excitement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:58.080
as the rest of the world erupts in cheers and&nbsp;
happiness at the finale of the Truman Show.
&nbsp;

